          "title": "You'll want to know: обида",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обида (obída) — \"hurt feelings, offence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Он до сих пор помнит эту обиду. On do sikh pór pómnit étu obídu. He still remembers that hurt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Не в обиду — no offence meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обида (obída) is inherited from Proto-Slavic obvida (EtymDB), derived from obviděti, which is built on ob- and viděti 'to see'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
