          "title": "You'll want to know: обижаться",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обижаться (obizhátsya) — \"to take offence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Она часто обижается на мои шутки. Oná chásto obizháyetsya na moí shútki. She often takes offence at my jokes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; the perfective is обидеться (обижусь, обидишься). Обижаться на кого — to be offended with someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обижаться (obizhátsya) is the reflexive of обижать (obizhát), the imperfective partner of обидеть; all three share the root of обида (obída) 'offence', from Proto-Slavic obvida (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
