          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "прощать (proshchát) is the imperfective partner of простить 'to forgive'; EtymDB links it to Old East Slavic prostiti, and both verbs are usually traced to простой 'simple, free', so to forgive is to set someone free."
            }
          ]
        },
